From beb03b396c125735ee2188bb9d9030006976fb9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-port <linux-port@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:20:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(desktop): give the Linux shell macOS-like window
 behaviour

Linux previously fell through the desktop policy gate and quit with its last
window, so a package built for it could not start.

- policy: allow Linux x64/arm64 instead of throwing; the mandatory-update
  policy stays inert without a feed
- lifecycle: keep the application and its tasks alive when the last window
  closes, matching macOS, while Windows keeps exiting
- window: reuse the window-controls overlay (the same mechanism Windows
  uses) so the page owns the titlebar area; DSH_DESKTOP_LINUX_NATIVE_FRAME=1
  restores the desktop frame
- preloads: reserve the caption area and relay fullscreen state on Linux
- menu/locale: give Linux its own quit label
- tests: assert the new Linux behaviour
